A||||14||86SE||What?? No rev limiter??||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||08-13-2000||03:37 PM||||I checked to see if my 2.8 has a rev limiter the other night.  It reved clear up to 6500 (so the tach says) and did not shut off.  It did let out 4 nice bluish orange 15" flames out the rear thoe!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  It was cool....<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||08-13-2000||04:11 PM||||None of the 86 and up calibrators have rev limits or speed limiters although I've heard that a few early one's did. Never seen one. The limiters are set to:<P>RPM 655360 (On)  1.31072E+006 (Off)<BR>MPH 255 (On) 254 (Off)<P>It think we can consider those to be effectively disabled.       <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||08-13-2000||04:13 PM||||I'm sory if I sound rude, But that Is the WORST WAY I have EVER heard of to check the rev limiter.||||reg||4
Z||000003||EdsB52||08-13-2000||05:40 PM||||Ya! The rev limiter would be a rod going through the trunk lid!||||reg||1
Z||000004||pHoOl||08-13-2000||05:54 PM||||How exactly did you shoot flames out your pipes?  that'd be cool, but i thought that you'd have to modify it to do it<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||08-13-2000||07:55 PM||||the flames are sweet.. GT Bastards car (the SE) on the dyno at 7200 winding down would do the same... ||||reg||1
Z||000006||pHoOl||08-13-2000||08:44 PM||||do they just happen naturally when you run that high?  or is it only in neutral?  cause i always thought it'd be cool to kill a Mudstain and then kick some flames on as you flew past just to rub it in a little.  (not burning his car, I know that would not be good)  Will it happen if you're in Drive on my little three speed, and redline?||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||08-13-2000||08:54 PM||||the rpms do have a bit to do with it but more than not it's the igniting of unburned fuel in the exhaust system.. in order to have unburn fuel you'll need to take your cat off... the cat burns this fuel for better emissions... i can send you a movie of a Formula Mazda at 16,000rpm doing this same thing.. from 4k to off the throttle winding down... ||||reg||1
Z||000008||86SE||08-14-2000||02:30 AM||||Possibly it was the worst way, but for me the quickest!  Took exactly 2.019 seconds to find out.<P>And hey, I still have all 6 rods all in 1 piece, and I highly doubt a rod will go UP, its most likely to go straight down throught the oil pan (like a bomb in the engine) spewing extremely hot motor oil (remember, the engine is turning at a rate of 108.3 revolutions per second) onto the exhaust pipes instantly ignighting and in another 2 seconds the rear of the car would have been engulped in flames.......Hehehehe, I know the concequences  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>About the flame thing, just rev it to around 4500 and let up off the throttle, then around 2500 BOOM 4 big flames shoot out!!  Its gathers quite a crowd..  And you have to make sure you don't have a cat converter, im not sure if it would work if you had one on.<P>And I was thinking the EXACT same thing.  There is a green 97-99 V6 Mustang around town, and I know I can take it.  I want to race him then throw some flames in his direction.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||10
Z||000009||Phil||08-14-2000||06:44 AM||||Flames? Did someone say flames?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Flames.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||HugGRRRFiero||08-14-2000||09:55 AM||||Wow...   For us 4-cylinder guys, you could drill a hole in your tips, screw in a sparkplug, hook it up to a coil, let the engine run a bit rich, and flip a switch to get the same effect.  Just make sure the car behind you isn't too close  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000011||JohnnyK||08-14-2000||02:33 PM||||Why wouldn't that work for a 6 cyl? (I have a 4cyl, I'm just curious)||||reg||1
Z||000012||pHoOl||08-16-2000||12:36 AM||||I'd imagine that it would work.  My other idea had been to hook up some sort of alternate fuel source for the flames.  I haven't figured it all out yet (what you would burn, what to contain it in, what to deliver it to the pipes) but i was thinking that if you had some other sort of fuel source (I.E. dumping raw fuel on the pipes in a controlled location) you could achive the same effect without too much modification.  Like  i said, i haven't thought all of this out, and by no means have tried it.  So if what i'm saying is actually going to make a Fiero S'more, try not to flame me too much.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Standard||08-16-2000||04:38 AM||||I've been told that my GT gets some flames when I shift after full throttle acceleration.. I figured it was the WOT fuel enrichment and the lack of a cat.. close the throttle quickly, some raw fuel gets dumped down the exhaust and it ignites when it mixes with oxygen at the tips.. I don't know if my car will flame when I rev it in neutral or not.. maybe I'll have to go and find out.. hehe   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>On a related note, would the lack of a cat cause the exhaust to "pop" more between shifts and when I close the throttle? or is it just the short exhuast system?  The only other car I've heard that does that was a Porsche.. I'm definatly not complaining, just wondering..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 149,000 miles and counting!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 08-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||1FST2M6||08-16-2000||08:52 AM||||the lack of cat will cause your car to pop.. it's fuel burning in the exhaust.. (my SE did that after i ditched the cat) with the 2.5" Random Cat i had it was a lot quieter and not nearly as SCARRY sounding... but taking the cat off lost some torque! so there is a trade off.  ---cool sound--- or ---more torque--- it wans't enough torque for me to really care i opted for the SWEET sound and comprssion braking pop! A mustang with an H-pipe or Basani x-pipe will also have this pop... anything with a manual tranny and no cat ||||reg||1
